```
Then crew job methods. Could add all crew logic near staffSpots or before drawStaff. Let's implement in one block near staff functions (after drawStaffTags maybe). But first need add methods used by constructor/draw.

`enqueueCrewJob`:
```
  enqueueCrewJob(id, propId, index, kind, extra = {}) {
    const g = this.game;
    if (!g.state.staff.includes(id)) return false;
    if (propId !== g.state.activeProperty) return false;
    this.ensureCrew(g.propConfig);
    const st = this.crewStates.get(id);
    if (!st) return false;
    // One queued job per pot/kind; drop duplicate backlog.
    const pending = st.job && st.job.index === index && st.job.kind === kind;
    if (pending || st.queue.some(j => j.index === index && j.kind === kind)) return true;
    st.queue.push({ propId, index, kind, ...extra });
    if (st.queue.length > 6) st.queue.shift();
    return true;
  }
```
`ensureCrew(p)` should not reset if property same. It creates state for hired. Called from updateCrew and enqueue. However if called from event before draw and property change? okay.
Maybe `ensureCrew` also deletes states not hired. fine.

But if queue length >6 shift removes job whose hidden plant/ghost we set. We need clean those:
```
if (st.queue.length > 6) { const dropped=st.queue.shift(); this.cleanupJobVisual(dropped); }
```
Could implement `releaseJobArtifacts(job)`. Also `st.job` not dropped. Keep queue 6 unlikely. Simpler don't cap; events won't accumulate beyond ~1-2. No cap.

`ensureCrew(p)`:
```
  ensureCrew(p) {
    if (this.crewPropId !== p.id) {
      this.crewPropId = p.id;
      this.crewStates.clear();
      this.hiddenPlants.clear();
      this.trimGhosts.clear();
    }
    const hired = this.game.state.staff;
    for (const id of [...this.crewStates.keys()]) if (!hired.includes(id)) this.crewStates.delete(id);
    const spots = this.staffSpots(p);
    for (const id of hired) {
      if (!STAFF_BY_ID[id] || !spots[id]) continue;
      if (!this.crewStates.has(id)) this.crewStates.set(id, this.makeCrewState(id, spots[id]));
      else this.crewStates.get(id).home = spots[id];
    }
    this.cleanupCrewArtifacts(p);
  }
```
Should ensure crew states persist across property switch? Currently clears and respawns at homes in new room. Fine. But clearing queue on switch loses jobs; auto timers continue; next jobs appear. Hidden plants/ghost cleared. Good.

Property switch resets all to home. Nice.

`makeCrewState`:
